  "description": "Maintain drum water level by delivering feedwater at flow above evaporation rate and at head above boiler pressure plus valve/piping losses; NPSH available must exceed pump NPSH required at hot feedwater temperature to avoid cavitation. Arrangements: direct feed per boiler or booster set feeding a common manifold with modulating feedwater valves.",
  "specifications": [
    {
      "metric": "Applicability of the 16-step selection method",
      "unit": "boiler horsepower; design pressure 150-500 psig",
      "basis": "HPAC Engineering article by Steve Connor (Cleaver-Brooks) and Jim Swetye (Grundfos)",
      "source": {
        "url": "https://www.hpac.com/heating/article/20928645/16-steps-to-proper-boiler-feed-pump-selection",
        "source_id": "hpac-com-20928645-16-steps-to-proper-boiler-feed-pump-selection"
      },
      "low": 100,
      "high": 1200
    },
    {
      "metric": "Base flow formula",
      "unit": "gpm (as presented)",
      "basis": "HPAC article step 2; 0.069 is a stated constant",
      "source": {
        "url": "https://www.hpac.com/heating/article/20928645/16-steps-to-proper-boiler-feed-pump-selection",
        "source_id": "hpac-com-20928645-16-steps-to-proper-boiler-feed-pump-selection"
      },
      "value": "boiler maximum-capacity HP x 0.069 x C; C=1.50 intermittent, C=1.15 continuous"
    },
    {
      "metric": "Continuous blowdown and bypass allowance",
      "unit": "percent of pump best-efficiency-point flow",
      "basis": "HPAC steps 3-4: continuous blowdown often ~10% of BEP flow; bypass recirculation often 10-20% of BEP flow",
      "source": {
        "url": "https://www.hpac.com/heating/article/20928645/16-steps-to-proper-boiler-feed-pump-selection",
        "source_id": "hpac-com-20928645-16-steps-to-proper-boiler-feed-pump-selection"
      },
      "low": 10,
      "high": 20
    },
    {
      "metric": "Base head formula",
      "unit": "feet of head",
      "basis": "HPAC step 6; factor 1.03 is the safety margin on boiler pressure",
      "source": {
        "url": "https://www.hpac.com/heating/article/20928645/16-steps-to-proper-boiler-feed-pump-selection",
        "source_id": "hpac-com-20928645-16-steps-to-proper-boiler-feed-pump-selection"
      },
      "value": "max boiler operating pressure x 2.31 x 1.03 / liquid specific gravity"
    },
    {
      "metric": "Shutoff head above safety-valve setting",
      "unit": "percent",
      "basis": "HPAC steps 10 and 14; shutoff head must be at least 3% above safety-valve setting",
